# AddressSanitizer suppressions for DOLFINx DeveloperDebug builds.
#
# Use with: ASAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<path-to-this-file>
#
# container-overflow suppressions are typically better handled with
# ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_container_overflow=0, since they arise from
# std::vector/std::string built by a non-instrumented dependency (Catch2,
# spdlog, ADIOS2, PETSc) and touched by instrumented DOLFINx code, not from a
# real bug.
